### Example in Your Flow System

Let’s integrate structured output into your `NoInternetFlow` to return a diagnostic result:

#### Updated `NoInternetFlow.java`

```java
package com.example.flow;

import com.example.service.DynamicPromptService;
import com.example.service.KnowledgeStore;
import com.example.service.LlmService;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Qualifier;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;

@Component
public class NoInternetFlow extends BaseFlow {

    private static final String FLOW_IDENTIFIER = "no_internet";
    private static final String PROMPT_TEXT = "Diagnose and suggest fixes for:";
    private static final String TEMPLATE_NAME = "basic";

    public NoInternetFlow(@Qualifier("teamBKnowledgeStore") KnowledgeStore teamBKnowledgeStore) {
        super(FLOW_IDENTIFIER, PROMPT_TEXT, null, teamBKnowledgeStore, TEMPLATE_NAME);
    }

    public record DiagnosticResult(String issue, String status, List<String> fixes) {}

    @Override
    public String execute(String userInput, String sessionId, DynamicPromptService promptService, LlmService llmService) {
        String apiResult = simulateNetworkCheck(userInput);
        String dynamicPrompt = promptService.buildPrompt(
            userInput + "\nAPI Result: " + apiResult + "\nReturn a JSON object with issue, status, and fixes (array of strings).",
            null, getTemplateName(), getVectorStore(), getKnowledgeStore(), sessionId
        );
        String finalPrompt = getPromptText() + "\n" + dynamicPrompt;

        // Use ChatClient directly for structured output
        ChatClient chatClient = ChatClient.builder(llmService.getChatModel()).build();
        DiagnosticResult result = chatClient.prompt()
            .user(finalPrompt)
            .call()
            .entity(DiagnosticResult.class);

        return "Issue: " + result.issue() + ", Status: " + result.status() + ", Fixes: " + String.join("; ", result.fixes());
    }

    private String simulateNetworkCheck(String userInput) {
        return "Network status: Router offline";
    }
}
```

#### Sample Output
- AI Response (JSON): `{"issue": "No internet", "status": "Router offline", "fixes": ["Restart router", "Check cables"]}`
- Java Output: `DiagnosticResult[issue=No internet, status=Router offline, fixes=[Restart router, Check cables]]`
- Final String: `"Issue: No internet, Status: Router offline, Fixes: Restart router; Check cables"`

